From e3e33d0f2cf8d6a92df69c2b6522091a754f4164 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:57:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: b53: clear the flow accelerator trap ports before
 the rules

b53_fa_trap_clear() turns the CFP rules off and clears them before it
resets fa_trap_ports. During that time b53_fa_trap_active() still
reports the traps as on, so a TCP or IPv6 flow can be offloaded after
its rules are gone. It then runs without them until the next stats poll
takes it out, as the flows offloaded before the clear do.

Clear fa_trap_ports first, so that no new flow is admitted once the
rules start to go, and write it with WRITE_ONCE(), as
b53_fa_trap_active() reads it with READ_ONCE(). A flow whose check ran
just before the clear can still be offloaded; the re-check in
bgmac_fa_flow_allowed() takes it out with the others.

With a test build on an RT-N18U, b53_fa_trap_clear() took 160 us in
each of ten runs, which is how long the window was. In a test build that
stretched the clear to 2 s, a TCP flow that started during it was
offloaded and ran without the traps until the next stats poll. With this
change it stayed in software.

Signed-off-by: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
@@ -744,10 +744,10 @@ static void b53_fa_trap_clear(struct b53
 	static const u32 zero[B53_CFP_NUM_KEY_REGS];
 	int i;
 
+	WRITE_ONCE(dev->fa_trap_ports, 0);
 	b53_write8(dev, B53_CFP_PAGE, B53_CFP_CTRL, 0);
 	for (i = 0; i < B53_FA_TRAP_NUM; i++)
 		b53_cfp_write_tcam(dev, i, zero, zero);
-	dev->fa_trap_ports = 0;
 }
 
 /* The flow accelerator in front of port 8 forwards the frames of the
@@ -803,7 +803,7 @@ static void b53_fa_trap_update(struct b5
 
 	b53_write8(dev, B53_CFP_PAGE, B53_CFP_CTRL, src);
 	dev->fa_trap_port = trap;
-	dev->fa_trap_ports = src;
+	WRITE_ONCE(dev->fa_trap_ports, src);
 	dev_info(ds->dev, "flow accelerator traps to port %d\n", trap);
 }
 
